{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## (Result [23]|The fork|.*anchor)|without_previous|hidden.flags|noprev'\"' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md | sed -n '125,280p'; rg -n '\"'^## D198|''^## D199'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:148:## The fork probe (written before any send)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:172:  - **Requests.** The same 48 final requests, sent without the previous conclusion (`without_previous`). Its \"[Previous conclusion,\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:174:  - **Arms.** v7-noprev and J2b-noprev, 3 repeats each (288 calls). J2a is left out: it equalled v7 on rungs.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:180:    - If v7-noprev moves at least 8 more targets off the rejected rung than v7 does, and no more than 2 controls, the carried conclusion\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:182:    - If v7-noprev is within 3 targets of v7, the anchor is not what holds them: the errors are the judge's on this evidence.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:183:    - J2b-noprev against v7-noprev is J2b's effect without the anchor.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:191:## Result 2: the frozen judgement gold, rule (c) (51 requests × 3, scored by the frozen scorer's rule)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:219:## Result 3: the anchor test, v7 with and without the previous conclusion (the same 48 final requests, 3 repeats each)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:220:| Group | Role | n | Moved in at least 2 of 3: v7 | Moved: v7-noprev |\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:129:def without_previous(user):\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:149:        user = without_previous(user)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:158:    \"\"\"(system text, schema order or None) of an arm; 'v7' is the frozen judge as stored; a '-noprev' suffix names the same arm sent\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:160:    arm = arm[:-len('-noprev')] if arm.endswith('-noprev') else arm\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:230:        response = transport('openai', rebuild(request, system, order, strip_previous=arm.endswith('-noprev')))\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:321:        response = transport('openai', rebuild(request, system, order, strip_previous=arm.endswith('-noprev')))\n   125\t## Result 1: the final-request probe (2026-11-20, $1.21 spent of $3)\n   126\t| Arm | Targets moved off the stored rung in at least 2 of 3 repeats | Controls moved | Refused by the production check (of 144) |\n   127\t|---|---|---|---|\n   128\t| v7 re-send | 2 (Q31 1→2, old-2 Q9 2→3) | 0 | 0 |\n   129\t| J2a, order only | 2 (the same two) | 0 | 0 |\n   130\t| J2b, order plus check | 3 (the same two, plus old-2 Q16 1→3) | 0 | 0 |\n   131\t\n   132\t- **The registered falsifier fired at the rung level:** J2a moves no more targets than v7's re-send. J2b adds one.\n   133\t- **The derivations, read by Claude for 4 cases** (old-2 Q29, old-3 Q33, old-3 Q3, old-2 Q6), are unchanged under J2b:\n   134\t  - it still adds $25B and $18B;\n   135\t  - it still stacks the uplift;\n   136\t  - it still scales NVIDIA's $1.3T, now naming it a proxy.\n   137\t- **On M08 the material is ambiguous.** The items say \"$25 billion of equity investment commitments as of July 26\" and \"$18 billion\n   138\t  committed … for the remainder of FY2027\", with no stated relation. The readers' \"likely overlaps\" is an analyst's inference.\n   139\t- **The probe was confounded, and this was found before the slice, not at the end.**\n   140\t  - Every final request carries \"[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung N; reasons: …\", which is the rejected answer with its\n   141\t    whole derivation.\n   142\t  - The rejected rung had been held for a median of about 10 judgements: 1 to 46, and Q4 for 42.\n   143\t  - So the probe measures whether the judge overturns its own carried conclusion, not whether it would have chosen it.\n   144\t  - **The planned slice has the same flaw:** it starts from the 09-06 copy, with every earlier wrong rung carried in.\n   145\t- **The 432-card reading is deferred** (to be agreed). With the rungs unchanged, rule (a)'s floor of 12 needs the readers to support at\n   146\t  least 9 answers at a rung they rejected, on unchanged derivations. The reading cannot change the decision.\n   147\t\n   148\t## The fork probe (written before any send)\n   149\t- **Cases.** Per target, the stored judgement at which the rejected rung was first chosen and then held to the end. 6 are a question's\n   150\t  first judgement, with no previous conclusion. 18 are moves from another rung, where the previous conclusion is the rung before the\n   151\t  error. All 24 fork requests rebuild byte for byte.\n   152\t- **Arms.** v7, J2a and J2b, 3 repeats each: 216 calls, about $0.45.\n   153\t- **Metric (code).** A target \"repeats the rejected rung\" when its fork answer gives that rung in at least 2 of 3 repeats. Production\n   154\t  refusals are counted.\n   155\t- **Rule.**\n   156\t  - **If v7 at the fork repeats the rejected rung on 12 or more of 24**, the errors are the judge's, not a sample carried forward. An\n   157\t    arm passes the screen when it repeats on at least 8 fewer targets than v7, with no more refusals. Its fork answers and v7's are then\n   158\t    read blind by both families (216 cards plus plants) to confirm that the new rungs are supported.\n   159\t  - **If v7 at the fork repeats on 11 or fewer**, the errors are mostly one unlucky sample that the carried previous conclusion keeps.\n   160\t    The lever is then the anchor (how the previous conclusion is shown), not a reasoning check. J2a and J2b stop, and the anchor is\n   161\t    designed next.\n   162\t  - **If neither arm passes the screen while v7 repeats on 12 or more**, J2's levers do not fix these errors even without the anchor.\n   163\t    The J2 line stops and goes to Alex with this census.\n   164\t\n   165\t## Council F (`council-f-codex.md`, DISAGREE) and what follows\n   166\t- **The fork probe is dropped.** Its evidence differs from the final request's, and an error can predate the first use of the rejected\n   167\t  rung: old-2 Q29's earlier answer already adds $25B and $18B. The fork cannot isolate the anchor.\n   168\t- **The 432-card reading runs** before either arm is called passed or failed. Reasoning can be repaired at an unchanged rung (rule\n   169\t  (a)), and support can be lost at an unchanged rung (rule (b)). The deck was built on 2026-11-20: 432 answers plus 3 confirmed\n   170\t  plants, 0 invalid rungs.\n   171\t- **The anchor test** (written before its results).\n   172\t  - **Requests.** The same 48 final requests, sent without the previous conclusion (`without_previous`). Its \"[Previous conclusion,\n   173\t    for comparison only] …\" block goes, and so does the \"[Not shown: N more pieces … the previous conclusion carries them]\" line.\n   174\t  - **Arms.** v7-noprev and J2b-noprev, 3 repeats each (288 calls). J2a is left out: it equalled v7 on rungs.\n   175\t  - **Flag.** 34 of 48 requests had hidden pieces that the previous conclusion carried; without it they lose that information. Results\n   176\t    are reported apart for those 34 and for the 14 clean requests.\n   177\t  - **Metric (code).** Targets moved off the rejected rung in at least 2 of 3 repeats; controls moved off their supported rung in at\n   178\t    least 2 of 3. Each is compared with the same arm sent with the previous conclusion.\n   179\t  - **Reading.**\n   180\t    - If v7-noprev moves at least 8 more targets off the rejected rung than v7 does, and no more than 2 controls, the carried conclusion\n   181\t      holds the errors in place. The lever is then the anchor.\n   182\t    - If v7-noprev is within 3 targets of v7, the anchor is not what holds them: the errors are the judge's on this evidence.\n   183\t    - J2b-noprev against v7-noprev is J2b's effect without the anchor.\n   184\t    - Moved answers are read blind before any claim of improvement.\n   185\t- **The end-to-end test is redefined** (council F agrees). It is a judge-only replay of the whole window from 07-01, with old's links,\n   186\t  sources and relations fixed. Each arm builds its own conclusions, citations, theme effects and queue.\n   187\t  - It runs on the prodpath machinery, extended from two days to the whole window.\n   188\t  - The cost is about $2 per draw and arm, from archived tokens.\n   189\t  - It replaces the slice from the 09-06 copy, which carried every earlier wrong rung.\n   190\t\n   191\t## Result 2: the frozen judgement gold, rule (c) (51 requests × 3, scored by the frozen scorer's rule)\n   192\t| Arm | Agreement per repeat (of 51) | Mean | Strict (refused counted as not agreeing) | Refused (of 153) | Rule (c): mean no lower than v7's |\n   193\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   194\t| v7 re-send | 45, 46, 44 | 45.0 | 45, 46, 42 (44.3) | 3 | — |\n   195\t| J2a | 44, 44, 45 | 44.3 | 43, 44, 45 (44.0) | 1 | **missed** |\n   196\t| J2b | 44, 45, 45 | 44.7 | 44, 44, 44 (44.0) | 2 | **missed** |\n   197\t\n   198\t- **The questions that differ, read with their reasons.**\n   199\t  - Five are single-repeat flips on boundary questions: d1-q17 and d3-q17 (China share), d2-q08 (H200 authorization), d2-q22 and\n   200\t    d3-q22 (FY2028 revenue).\n   201\t  - **One is a consistent J2b regression: d3-q18**, Kyber NVL144 shipping by the end of 2027. The gold says No (the reported slip to\n   202\t    2028). v7 says No in 2 of 3 repeats; J2b says Yes in 3 of 3. J2b's reasons treat the slip report as \"one underlying source\", weigh\n   203\t    NVIDIA's denial, and name the NVL576 statement \"a proxy\". The scope row was read as a reason to discount specific third-party\n   204\t    evidence. That is the direction council A warned of.\n   205\t- **Both arms miss (c) as written.** The gaps are within one question of 51, inside v7's own repeat range of 44–46. The miss stands as\n   206\t  scored.\n   207\t\n   208\t## The whole-window production path (validated at $0)\n   209\t- `window old-2 replay`: a copy holding nothing before 07-01. Each day is fed old's links, evidence, sources, relations, opened\n   210\t  questions, closures and successions. The judge's own round runs from production's own queue.\n   211\t- Result over 82 days: the same judged set on 82 of 82 days, the same evidence in 1,616 of 1,616 requests, and 1,612 of 1,616 requests\n   212\t  byte-identical.\n   213\t- The 4 differences are retries. In old's run, a refused first answer was re-asked with \"The code returned the previous answer\n   214\t  because …\". The replay answers the first request with old's accepted retry answer, so no retry note is sent.\n   215\t- The machinery for the end-to-end judge test is ready.\n   216\t- **Cost correction.** The whole window is about 1,616 judge calls per draw, at about $0.002 each: **about $3.3 per draw and arm**, not\n   217\t  $2. The $2.04 figure was the 14-day window for two draws.\n   218\t\n   219\t## Result 3: the anchor test, v7 with and without the previous conclusion (the same 48 final requests, 3 repeats each)\n   220\t| Group | Role | n | Moved in at least 2 of 3: v7 | Moved: v7-noprev |\n   221\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n   222\t| Clean (no hidden pieces) | targets | 8 | 1 | 3 |\n   223\t| Clean | controls | 6 | 0 | 1 |\n   224\t| Hidden pieces carried by the previous conclusion | targets | 16 | 1 | 11 |\n   225\t| Hidden pieces | controls | 18 | 0 | 1 |\n   226\t| **All** | **targets** | **24** | **2** | **14** |\n   227\t| **All** | **controls** | **24** | **0** | **2** |\n   228\t\n   229\t- **The registered reading fires:** 12 more targets moved (at least 8 needed), and 2 controls (at most 2 allowed). The carried\n   230\t  conclusion holds the errors in place, so the lever is the anchor, not a reasoning check.\n   231\t- **The direction of the moves (Claude's code read against both readers' named rung):**\n   232\t  - 2027 capex: 4→3 on all three draws' questions (the readers named rung 3);\n   233\t  - equity commitments (M08): 3→2 and 3→1 (readers: rungs 1–2);\n   234\t  - FY2027 revenue: 1→2 (readers: rung 2);\n   235\t  - total CPU: 1→2;\n   236\t  - FY2028 gross margin: 3→2;\n   237\t  - Vera FY2028: 3→2;\n   238\t  - states' moratoriums: 2→1 (readers: zero states).\n   239\t\n   240\t  These are a code reading only. The registered blind reading of the moved answers is owed before any claim.\n   241\t- **The controls that moved:** C-new-3-Q33 4→5 (3/3), and C-old-2-Q15 5→{2,4,5}. To be read.\n   242\t- **The confound, measured.** In the hidden-piece requests the previous conclusion carries many pieces: 13 to 82 per question, and\n   243\t  2,264 for FY2027 revenue. Every item the rejected answer cited is in the shown set, so the moved answers had the evidence the\n   244\t  error was built from. The previous derivation and the hidden pieces are removed together, though, so their effects are not\n   245\t  separated. Only 8 clean targets exist, with +2 moves.\n   246\t- **This bears on D198** (Alex, 2026-10-27: a judgement reads the evidence in view; \"the previous conclusion carries\" the rest). The\n   247\t  carrier is also what keeps a wrong derivation alive for a median of 8.5 judgements.\n2559:## D198 · 2026-10-27 · A judgement reads the evidence in view, not everything in force\n2568:## D199 · 2026-10-27 · One extraction call stays; its gate rule becomes decidable and the empty-answer exit goes (v16, poc-v32)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
