{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2554,2570p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py | sed -n '117,166p;219,242p;342,362p;580,635p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt | sed -n '1,12p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '26,52p;121,163p'\"","aggregated_output":"  2554\t- The class ($0, `docs/research/2026-10-27-shared-quantity/proof.py`): every AI-capex aggregate candidate of r3, r4 and r5 (9, 11, 11) against the theses that existed before it. r3 (no collision judge) opened six 2026 aggregates; r4 and r5, with the judge, each opened one duplicate: the judge read \"Big Tech AI outlays\" against \"the top five's total capex\" (r4 seq 351) and \"the five named companies' capex\" against \"industrywide AI infrastructure spending\" (r5 seq 200) as distinct questions in one matter, and later candidates then merged into the duplicate (r4: two). The contract already says what identity is: `industry_aggregate` is \"one aggregate quantity for one calendar year … another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\" (role-v12), and D155 puts identity in code where it is fully determined.\n  2555\t- Decided: a candidate admitted as `industry_aggregate` / `shared_quantity` with a quantity measure is keyed by (theme, measure, period) with no scope (`identity.automatic_key`); the writer records its key with `scope_source = 'shared'`; on the Jev path code decides its destination before any judge (`jev_matching.shared_quantity_target`): the open thesis of the same key is the same thesis (merge), the latest earlier period without a successor is its predecessor (succession), otherwise new. Policy stages and other events keep their event-typed identity; a company's own line (MSFT capex) is another object and never the aggregate; a theme quantity without the admission reason (the pre-D184 financing-amount case of T4) stays the model's. Tests: `tests/test_shared_quantity.py` (3, red first), suite 187.\n  2556\t- Proof on stored data: the rule flips every duplicate to a merge (r3: 5 merges + 1 succession; r4: 1; r5: 1), touches no other object, and changes no stored matching check (preflight C: 618 judged, 9 refused, as before). Small-scale validation (Alex: no full rerun): the r5 window replayed with extraction pinned to r5's answers and matching live (`docs/research/2026-10-27-shared-quantity/pinned_arm.py`, `poc/data/pinned-shared-2026-10-27/`): one 2026 aggregate thesis (v22, 33 evidence links; r5 had two theses with 40 links between them) and one 2027 successor (v29, succeeding v22); the rule decided 10 aggregate candidates (8 merges, 1 succession, 1 opened), the collision judge was asked 17 times about other peers, cost $0.21 (Jev) + $0.01 (judge).\n  2557\t- Codex read-only review of the branch's code (D195–D197, `scratchpad codex-code-review-d195-d197.out.md`), seven findings, each fixed with a failing test first: an unknown measure (`other`) is never a shared identity; two wordings of the next year's aggregate in one answer are one successor (coalesced by key, not refused as a second successor); a shared candidate's comparison list holds every thesis of its theme and measure, so a predecessor outside the search window is a valid target; the judgement's theme ids are checked against the block the request carried, not the ledger's state at check time; Jev is not asked a relation question about a shared candidate; a ledger written before the theme block gains the column at the write boundary (test that fails without the migration); one propagation rule (`queued_by_change`) serves live and resumed rounds. Suite 192.\n  2558\t\n  2559\t## D198 · 2026-10-27 · A judgement reads the evidence in view, not everything in force\n  2560\t\n  2561\t- Alex, 2026-10-27, on the finding that evidence in force grows without bound (v6, NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center revenue: 574 pieces after six weeks, 415 never cited by any of its 33 judgements; 40 of 316 judge requests over 30k tokens, max 67k; judging 38% of spend and rising; the run's stall came from enumerating 300+ ids): \"这是什么问题你深度思考之后改\".\n  2562\t- What the problem is (design: `docs/research/2026-10-27-evidence-in-view/design.md`): two mechanisms. (1) Extraction links wide: `role-v14.txt` says \"every statement and number is, by default, evidence linked to a shown thesis\" and also \"link only to the thesis it directly concerns; omit statements with no thesis\"; the model attaches every business mention to the broadest thesis (2.5 pieces per item on v6; a liquid-cooling note, a SuperPOD purchase, a rack R&D story). Not changed here; the prompt audit is reported to Alex as the next slice. (2) Judging-v4 reads everything in force every time (\"Rejudge from all evidence currently in force\"); an analyst keeps what his view rests on and reads what arrived.\n  2563\t- Decided: from judging-v5 (`poc-v30`) a judgement of a thesis is shown, of its evidence in force, the arrivals (pieces linked after the thesis's fifth most recent judgement, READINGS = 5; everything when it has fewer) and the basis (pieces cited by one of its last ten judgements, BASIS = 10). The rest stays in force in the ledger; the request names the count (\"[Not shown: N more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]\"); the answer may cite and push only shown ids, checked against the request that was sent (`judging.evidence_shown_in`, as the theme block is). Nothing leaves the ledger; the repeat / replace / new rules, \"in force\", the rejudgement triggers, eligibility, the theme block and dependencies are unchanged. Gated on the prompt version: v4 ledgers and configurations read in force as before.\n  2564\t- Measured ($0, `census.py`, two ledgers): among judgements after a thesis's first, the rule would have hidden 1.5% (nvda-3m) and 1.1% (r5) of the citations the judge actually made (22 of 325 and 7 of 261 judgements lose one cite, mostly third-party risk mentions listed in a \"pull the other way\" sentence); shown mean 95 and 109 pieces where in force averaged 225 and 178. Tighter rules hid 16% (cited last time + new since) or kept growing (ever cited + three readings). Arm beside control (`ab.py`, $0.03): v6, v11, v22 from the same ledger state, v4 fresh against v5: the same rung and `changed` on all three, reasons consistent, request tokens 76,476 → 12,516, 53,151 → 11,204, 25,806 → 8,425. Tests: `tests/test_evidence_in_view.py` (4, red first); suite 199.\n  2565\t- Applied to the three-month run at a day boundary: 2026-08-18 finished under `poc-v29` on the serial path (the parallel runner refuses a half-done day after a code change), `poc-v30` from 2026-08-19. Prompt `judging-v5` is `judging-v4` with the first rule reworded (2,264 → 2,437 characters; the growth is the sentence that says what is not shown and who carries it).\n  2566\t- Also in this slice, from the stall at 2026-08-07: a code-refused judgement answer is retired from the archive's lookup (`model.Archive.retire`; the row stays; schema-refused and malformed rows already carried a suffix), so a resume re-samples instead of replaying the refused answer; and the request's closing line names a closed set that exists (\"cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis\"; \"a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views\"): 4 of the run's 5 retried first answers had put theme ids into cites_views.\n  2567\t\n  2568\t## D199 · 2026-10-27 · One extraction call stays; its gate rule becomes decidable and the empty-answer exit goes (v16, poc-v32)\n  2569\t\n  2570\t- Alex, on the instability trace: \"不这个一次一定是可以搞过的 → 读明白，抽取 … 这一定是prompt 的问题，你如果再拆成两步这个消耗的luna calls 太多了\"; then \"你要反思自己的错误，然后下去改然后马上测试啊，不要一直diverge scope\". The two-call design (`docs/research/2026-10-27-two-step-extraction/design.md`, two review rounds) is recorded and not built.\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\tdef stored(case):\n   120\t    \"\"\"The latest stored judgement of the case's view and its archived request and answer.\"\"\"\n   121\t    views, archive = store_paths(case['draw'])\n   122\t    v = readonly(views)\n   123\t    j = v.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by seq desc limit 1', (case['view_id'],)).fetchone()\n   124\t    a = readonly(archive)\n   125\t    row = a.execute('select request_json, response_json, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256=? limit 1', (j['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()\n   126\t    return dict(j), json.loads(row['request_json']), json.loads(row['response_json']), json.loads(row['answer_json'])\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef without_previous(user):\n   130\t    \"\"\"The request's user text with the previous conclusion removed (council F: pair identical requests with and without it): the\n   131\t    \"[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] …\" block and the \"[Not shown: …; the previous conclusion carries them]\" line.\"\"\"\n   132\t    import re\n   133\t    start = user.find('\\n\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]')\n   134\t    if start >= 0:\n   135\t        end = user.find('\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema.', start)\n   136\t        assert end > start, 'the previous conclusion block runs to the closing sentence'\n   137\t        user = user[:start] + user[end:]\n   138\t    return re.sub(r'^\\[Not shown: \\d+ more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them\\]\\n?', '', user, flags=re.M)\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\tdef rebuild(stored_request, system_text, order=None, strip_previous=False):\n   142\t    \"\"\"The request as production builds it (model.build_request, key order and schema from code), with the given system text. With\n   143\t    `order`, the schema's properties are written in that order (the same fields and types; the model writes fields in this order).\"\"\"\n   144\t    from hivemind import config, model\n   145\t    from hivemind.views import judging\n   146\t    cfg = config.load(CONFIG)\n   147\t    user = stored_request['messages'][1]['content']\n   148\t    if strip_previous:\n   149\t        user = without_previous(user)\n   150\t    schema = judging.schema_for(cfg.rejudging.prompt_version)\n   151\t    if order is not None:\n   152\t        assert sorted(order) == sorted(schema['properties']), 'an order names exactly the schema fields'\n   153\t        schema['properties'] = {field: schema['properties'][field] for field in order}\n   154\t    return model.build_request(cfg.rejudging, system_text, user, schema, 'judgement', cfg.provider)\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\tdef arm_spec(arm):\n   158\t    \"\"\"(system text, schema order or None) of an arm; 'v7' is the frozen judge as stored; a '-noprev' suffix names the same arm sent\n   159\t    without the previous conclusion (see `strips_previous`).\"\"\"\n   160\t    arm = arm[:-len('-noprev')] if arm.endswith('-noprev') else arm\n   161\t    if arm == 'v7':\n   162\t        return FROZEN_SYSTEM.read_text(encoding='utf-8'), None\n   163\t    order_file = HERE / 'arms' / f'{arm}.order.json'\n   164\t    return (HERE / 'arms' / f'{arm}.txt').read_text(encoding='utf-8'), (json.loads(order_file.read_text()) if order_file.exists() else None)\n   165\t\n   166\t\n   219\t    \"\"\"Cents: each case's rebuilt request with the arm's system text, sent `repeats` times, each answer stored with its usage.\"\"\"\n   220\t    transport, ledger = transport_for(ledger_path)\n   221\t    system, order = arm_spec(arm)\n   222\t    rows = json.loads((OUT / 'cases.json').read_text())\n   223\t    folder = OUT / 'probe' / arm\n   224\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   225\t    jobs = [(case, k) for case in rows for k in range(1, repeats + 1)]\n   226\t\n   227\t    def one(job):\n   228\t        case, k = job\n   229\t        _, request, _, _ = stored(case)\n   230\t        response = transport('openai', rebuild(request, system, order, strip_previous=arm.endswith('-noprev')))\n   231\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   232\t        (folder / f\"{case['case']}-{k}.json\").write_text(json.dumps({'case': case, 'repeat': k, 'arm': arm, 'answer': json.loads(content),\n   233\t                                                                    'usage': response.get('usage')}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   234\t        return f\"{case['case']}-{k}\"\n   235\t\n   236\t    with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(WORKERS) as pool:\n   237\t        for name in pool.map(one, jobs):\n   238\t            print('probe', name, flush=True)\n   239\t    print('ledger', json.dumps(ledger.read()))\n   240\t\n   241\t\n   242\tdef gold_entries():\n   342\t    and the reference, implied outcome and reasons, labelled, the same way for every arm.\"\"\"\n   343\t    import re\n   344\t    text = (DIAG / 'deck' / f\"{case['card']}.txt\").read_text()\n   345\t    choices = re.findall(r'^(\\d+)\\. (.*)$', text.split('Possible answers', 1)[1].split('\\n\\n', 1)[0], re.M)\n   346\t    labels = {int(k): v for k, v in choices}\n   347\t    rung = answer['rung']\n   348\t    if rung not in labels:\n   349\t        return None\n   350\t    reason = f\"Reference: {answer['reference']} Implied outcome: {answer['implied_outcome']} Reasons: {answer['reasons']}\"\n   351\t    lines = text.split('\\n')\n   352\t    answer_line = next(i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if line.startswith('Latest answer at the cutoff: '))\n   353\t    assert lines[answer_line + 1].startswith('Reason given: ')\n   354\t    lines[answer_line] = f'Latest answer at the cutoff: {labels[rung]}'\n   355\t    lines[answer_line + 1] = f'Reason given: {reason}'\n   356\t    return '\\n'.join(lines), labels\n   357\t\n   358\t\n   359\tdef refusals_before(views_path, view_id, judgement_id, answer, request_text):\n   360\t    \"\"\"The production check's refusals of an answer (`judging.check_answer` against the request it answered) on the store as it stood\n   361\t    immediately before the stored judgement: later judgements are shadowed by a temporary table on a read-only connection (council C:\n   362\t    the stored final judgement is not the previous one).\"\"\"\n   580\t        mt.restore_closures(conn, PRODPATH_DRAW, all_views, seq)\n   581\t        conn.commit()\n   582\t        for j in judged:\n   583\t            results.append({'day': day, 'view': j['view_id'], 'rung': j['rung'], 'changed': j['changed'], 'queued_by_round': j['view_id'] not in scheduled})\n   584\t        judged_set = {j['view_id'] for j in judged}\n   585\t        print(json.dumps({'arm': arm, 'day': day, 'starting queue': len(scheduled), 'judged': len(judged),\n   586\t                          'added by the round': len(judged_set - set(scheduled)), 'same set as old': judged_set == old_judged,\n   587\t                          'old only': sorted(old_judged - judged_set), 'arm only': sorted(judged_set - old_judged)}), flush=True)\n   588\t    (folder / 'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(results, indent=1))\n   589\t    (folder / 'feed-log.json').write_text(json.dumps(log, indent=1))\n   590\t    if arm == 'replay':\n   591\t        checks = transport.checks\n   592\t        (folder / 'checks.json').write_text(json.dumps(checks, indent=1))\n   593\t        print('replay:', sum(c['same text'] for c in checks), 'of', len(checks), 'requests byte-identical to the archived ones;',\n   594\t              sum(c['same evidence shown'] for c in checks), 'show the same evidence')\n   595\t    else:\n   596\t        print('ledger', json.dumps(ledger.read()))\n   597\t\n   598\t\n   599\tdef probescore(arms=('v7', 'J2a', 'J2b')):\n   600\t    \"\"\"$0, after `read`: the locked decision rule (DESIGN-J2.md (a), (b), (d)) per arm against v7's re-send. Every arm x case x repeat\n   601\t    must be accounted for; an invalid-rung answer counts as refused and not supported. Jointly supported = both readers' final answer\n   602\t    mark is `supported` (a split is not).\"\"\"\n   603\t    key = json.loads(PROBE_KEY.read_text())\n   604\t    marks = json.loads((OUT / 'marks-probe.json').read_text())\n   605\t    rows = json.loads((OUT / 'cases.json').read_text())\n   606\t    supported, refused = {}, {}\n   607\t    for cid, m in marks.items():\n   608\t        if m['kind'] == 'plant':\n   609\t            continue\n   610\t        k = (m['arm'], m['case'], m['repeat'])\n   611\t        supported[k] = (m['marks'] or {}).get('answer') == 'supported'\n   612\t        refused[k] = bool(m.get('refusals'))\n   613\t    for m in key['invalid']:\n   614\t        k = (m['arm'], m['case'], m['repeat'])\n   615\t        supported[k], refused[k] = False, True\n   616\t    missing = [(a, c['case'], r) for a in arms for c in rows for r in (1, 2, 3) if (a, c['case'], r) not in supported]\n   617\t    if missing:\n   618\t        raise SystemExit(f'{len(missing)} answers not accounted for, e.g. {missing[:4]}: refused')\n   619\t    holds = {a: {c['case']: sum(supported[(a, c['case'], r)] for r in (1, 2, 3)) >= 2 for c in rows} for a in arms}\n   620\t    targets = [c['case'] for c in rows if c['role'] == 'target']\n   621\t    controls = [c['case'] for c in rows if c['role'] == 'control']\n   622\t    report = {}\n   623\t    for a in arms:\n   624\t        improved = [t for t in targets if holds[a][t] and not holds['v7'][t]]\n   625\t        worsened = [t for t in targets if holds['v7'][t] and not holds[a][t]]\n   626\t        lost = [c for c in controls if not holds[a][c]]\n   627\t        report[a] = {'targets held (>=2 of 3)': sum(holds[a][t] for t in targets), 'paired improved': improved, 'paired worsened': worsened,\n   628\t                     'net': len(improved) - len(worsened), 'controls lost': lost,\n   629\t                     'refused answers': sum(refused[(a, c['case'], r)] for c in rows for r in (1, 2, 3))}\n   630\t    for a in arms:\n   631\t        r = report[a]\n   632\t        verdict = '' if a == 'v7' else ('PASSES (a)(b)(d)' if r['targets held (>=2 of 3)'] >= 12 and r['net'] >= 8\n   633\t                                         and len(r['controls lost']) <= len(report['v7']['controls lost'])\n   634\t                                         and r['refused answers'] <= report['v7']['refused answers'] else 'does not pass (a)(b)(d)')\n   635\t        print(a, json.dumps(r), verdict)\n     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\n     4\t- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- “Themes in force” lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked “updated since this thesis was last judged” may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\n     9\t- Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n    10\t- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n    11\t- changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\n    26\t\n    27\tPUSHES = vocabulary.PUSHES\n    28\tSUPPORTED_VERSIONS = ('judging-v7',)   # D354: the frozen judging prompt\n    29\tREADINGS = 5                      # a piece is shown in the thesis's first five judgements after it arrives\n    30\tBASIS = 10                        # and while one of the last ten judgements cited it\n    31\tTHEME_REASONS_CHARS = 300\n    32\tUPDATED_MARK = 'updated since this thesis was last judged'\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef require_supported(prompt_version):\n    36\t    \"\"\"Refuses a judging prompt version this code does not build, before any request is made.\"\"\"\n    37\t    if prompt_version not in SUPPORTED_VERSIONS:\n    38\t        raise ValueError(f'judging {prompt_version!r} is not built; this code builds only {\", \".join(SUPPORTED_VERSIONS)} (D354)')\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef evidence_in_view(conn, view_id):\n    42\t    \"\"\"(the pieces a judgement of this thesis reads, how many pieces in force are not shown): the arrivals (linked after the\n    43\t    READINGS-th most recent judgement, or all when there are fewer) and the basis (cited by one of the last BASIS judgements),\n    44\t    both among the evidence in force.\"\"\"\n    45\t    in_force = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)\n    46\t    recent = store.recent_judgements(conn, view_id, BASIS)\n    47\t    arrivals_after = recent[READINGS - 1]['seq'] if len(recent) >= READINGS else -1\n    48\t    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\n    49\t    linked_at = {r['evidence_id']: r['seq'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))}\n    50\t    shown = [p for p in in_force if linked_at.get(p['evidence_id'], -1) > arrivals_after or p['evidence_id'] in basis]\n    51\t    return shown, len(in_force) - len(shown)\n    52\t\n   121\tdef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0):\n   122\t    \"\"\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown.\"\"\"\n   123\t    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}',\n   124\t             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n   125\t             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\n   126\t    if hidden:\n   127\t        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\n   128\t    for p in pieces:\n   129\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   130\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   131\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   132\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   133\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   134\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   135\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   136\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   137\t    if deps:\n   138\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   139\t        for d in deps:\n   140\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   141\t            if not target:\n   142\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   143\t                continue\n   144\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   145\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   146\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   147\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   148\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   149\t    if themes:\n   150\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   151\t        for theme in themes:\n   152\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   153\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   154\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   155\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   156\t    if last:\n   157\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   158\t    else:\n   159\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   160\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   161\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   162\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   163\t    return lines\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import judge_probe as p; c=next(c for c in json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"goldcases.json\\\").read_text()) if c[\\\"case\\\"]==\\\"G-d3-q18\\\"); a=p.readonly(p.GOLD_RUN/\\\"d3/archive.sqlite\\\"); s=json.loads(a.execute(\\\"select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=?\\\",(c[\\\"request_sha256\\\"],)).fetchone()[0])[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"]; print(s.splitlines()[0]); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(x for x in s.splitlines() if x.startswith(\\\"[Previous\\\"))); \nfor arm in (\\\"v7\\\",\\\"J2a\\\",\\\"J2b\\\"):\n for k in (1,2,3):\n  d=json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"goldprobe\\\"/arm/(\\\"G-d3-q18-{}.json\\\".format(k))).read_text()); print(arm,k,d[\\\"answer\\\"][\\\"rung\\\"],d[\\\"agrees\\\"],d[\\\"answer\\\"][\\\"reasons\\\"][:540])' ; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '4871,4890p;10125,10139p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import judge_probe as p; c=next(c for c in json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"goldcases.json\\\").read_text()) if c[\\\"case\\\"]==\\\"G-d3-q18\\\"); a=p.readonly(p.GOLD_RUN/\\\"d3/archive.sqlite\\\"); s=json.loads(a.execute(\\\"select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=?\\\",(c[\\\"request_sha256\\\"],)).fetchone()[0])[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"]; print(s.splitlines()[0]); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(x for x in s.splitlines() if x.startswith(\\\"[Previous\\\"))); \nfor arm in (\\\"v7\\\",\\\"J2a\\\",\\\"J2b\\\"):\n for k in (1,2,3):\n  d=json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"goldprobe\\\"/arm/(\\\"G-d3-q18-{}.json\\\".format(k))).read_text()); print(arm,k,d[\\\"answer\\\"][\\\"rung\\\"],d[\\\"agrees\\\"],d[\\\"answer\\\"][\\\"reasons\\\"][:540])' ; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '4871,4890p;10125,10139p'\"","aggregated_output":"Thesis v18 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Whether NVIDIA's Rubin Ultra generation (Kyber NVL144 racks) begins shipping by the end of calendar 2027\", 2027, due 2027-12-31): Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 1; reasons: The reference is NVIDIA’s stated 2027 roadmap for Rubin Ultra/Kyber, which sits at rung 1 (shipping by the deadline). The specific SemiAnalysis report of a slip to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing problems is meaningful counterevidence, but the repeated outlets are one underlying claim, not independent confirmations. NVIDIA has disputed the delay and specifically said Vera Rubin Ultra would scale to an NVL576 domain on its planned 2027 timeline; the newer statement that Rubin Ultra development remains on schedule is consistent with that position but adds no specific shipment evidence. The reported cancellation of the fallback weighs against the first-rung outcome, but does not establish that Kyber itself will miss the deadline. On balance, a 2027 start remains more likely than no\nv7 1 2 True The company’s stated 2027 roadmap is the reference and sits at rung 1 (Yes). On balance, the specific report of a greater-than-12-month Kyber delay to 2028, attributed to PCB midplane manufacturability problems, together with the reported cancellation of the fallback rack design, makes missing the deadline more likely. NVIDIA’s roadmap and 2027-timeline statements are meaningful counterevidence, but do not provide specific shipment evidence that outweighs that reported bottleneck. The bullish FY2027 Data Center revenue conclusion is c\nv7 2 2 True The reference is NVIDIA’s stated 2027 roadmap, which sits at rung 1 (Yes). The specific SemiAnalysis report says Kyber NVL144 has slipped by more than a year to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing problems, and its reported fallback was scrapped. That schedule-specific evidence outweighs NVIDIA’s general roadmap assurances and its statement that Vera Rubin Ultra will scale to an NVL576 domain on the planned 2027 timeline: the latter does not specifically confirm Kyber NVL144 shipments by the deadline. The implied start therefor\nv7 3 1 False The reference is NVIDIA’s stated 2027 roadmap, which is rung 1. SemiAnalysis’s specific report of a Kyber delay to 2028 and the reported cancellation of the fallback are meaningful downside evidence, but the repeated outlets are one underlying claim, not independent confirmation. NVIDIA has maintained that its roadmap is intact and specifically said Vera Rubin Ultra would scale to an NVL576 domain on its planned 2027 timeline; the evidence also includes a general expectation of a 2027 Kyber launch. On balance, a Kyber NVL144 shipping \nJ2a 1 2 True The specific reported delay and manufacturing cause, together with the loss of the fallback, outweigh NVIDIA's general roadmap assurance and its statement that Rubin Ultra would scale to NVL576 on the planned 2027 timeline; neither statement provides shipment evidence or directly resolves the reported Kyber midplane issue. The implied 2028 date crosses the only rung boundary, so the most likely outcome is rung 2 (No).\nJ2a 2 1 False The reported PCB midplane manufacturing difficulty and cancellation of the fallback design are concrete downside evidence, and the claimed delay to 2028 would cross the rung boundary. However, those delay reports trace to one SemiAnalysis claim, while NVIDIA has rejected the delay and stated that Vera Rubin Ultra will scale to NVL576 on its planned 2027 timeline. That is not proof of Kyber NVL144 shipments, but it leaves a 2027 start more likely than a miss. Recent repetitions of the same report and denial add no new fact.\nJ2a 3 2 True The reported delay is specific to the rack in question, gives a revised date and manufacturing cause, and the reported cancellation of the fallback weakens the prospect of shipping an alternative in 2027. I count the repeated SemiAnalysis coverage as one claim, not independent confirmation. NVIDIA’s “roadmap is intact” statement and planned 2027 NVL576 timeline support rung 1, but they are schedule assertions rather than evidence of volume in hand; on balance, the specific delay makes missing the deadline more likely. The v2 estimate \nJ2b 1 1 False The SemiAnalysis report of a delay to 2028, attributed to PCB midplane manufacturing problems, and the reported cancellation of the fallback design push toward rung 2. These are one underlying report, not independent confirmations. NVIDIA’s general roadmap statement is not decisive on its own, but its more specific 2027 NVL576 timeline and the statement that Rubin Ultra development remains on schedule support the 2027 outcome. The NVL576 plan is a target for a larger domain, not shipment volume in hand, so it is discounted rather than\nJ2b 2 1 False The specific SemiAnalysis report of a delay to 2028, attributed to PCB midplane manufacturing problems, and the reported cancellation of a fallback design weigh toward missing the deadline. However, these are claims from one underlying source, not independent confirmations; NVIDIA has disputed the delay, made a specific 2027 statement about Rubin Ultra scaling, and said Rubin Ultra development remains on schedule. The NVL576 statement is a proxy for the requested NVL144 shipment timing, not direct confirmation of it. On balance, the e\nJ2b 3 1 False The implied outcome is at the reference’s rung, so it does not cross the binary boundary. The detailed report of PCB midplane manufacturing problems and cancellation of the fallback design weighs meaningfully toward a miss, but it is one underlying third-party claim rather than independent confirmations; NVIDIA’s specific 2027 statement is stronger counterevidence than its generic “roadmap is intact” response. The bullish 2027 hyperscaler capex outlook supports demand and deployment incentives, but does not itself establish shipment t\n  4871\t## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n  4872\t\n  4873\t- **Alex, 2026-11-13** (unprompted, after a recap of the goal): \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\".\n  4874\t- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\n  4875\t- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n  4876\t- **Where written:** AGENTS.md, \"Authority and scope\" (the D439 bullet) and §7.3 \"Own the loop\"; `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`; the memory file `feedback-council-decides-while-alex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.\n  4877\t- **Scope:** all modules Alex has taken up; the current work is clean Step 1 (gates 2 and 3 of `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/COMBINED-PLAN.md`), then the Step 4 judgement faults that kept Stage B from passing.\n  4878\t\n  4879\t## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)\n  4880\t\n  4881\t- **Council** (D439; Alex not active): an independent Codex member and Claude argued four rounds (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mj-*`). Agreed facts: gate 2 failed under its declared rules (two stop lines on the memory article); the link line measured the wrong thing (c8's request returns an uncovered statement with empty links); the 3-of-9 against 0-of-9 memory-thesis difference is real and its cause is not established. The council's first position was to keep c8; Claude's was a larger re-send. The consensus, after Claude adopted the council's changes (a margin fixed in advance, a three-way result in which inconclusive is not a pass, retained statements decisive, an exercised-control rule, a named and simulation-validated interval): \"Council position: consensus on the rule in mj-challenge-2.md as amended by mj-challenge-3.md\" (`mj-codex-4.md`).\n  4882\t- **Decided:** the diagnostic in `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate2/MEMORY-DIAGNOSTIC.md` runs (108 sends, ceiling $2.0); its rule is `gate2/memory_rule.py`, frozen by sha256. c15yc goes on to gate 3's design only on \"proceed\" for both decisive outcomes; otherwise c8 stays and the council decides the next step. The gate-2 failure stays recorded.\n  4883\t- **Amended 2026-11-13 (council round mj-5, `council/mj-codex-5.md`: \"Council position: consensus on (a)\"):** the 11 jobs the $2.0 ceiling never sent are sent alone, same requests, under a $1.2 completion ceiling (a recorded departure from D440's step ceiling; the $40 total unchanged), before any diagnostic answer is read; the combined sample must hold 18 per arm per draw, or the diagnostic is inconclusive.\n  4884\t\n  4885\t## D441 · 2026-11-13 · The memory diagnostic does not let c15yc go on: the year change stops, c8 stays (rule fixed by council consensus, D440)\n  4886\t\n  4887\t- **Result** (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate2/MEMORY-RESULT.md`): memory-price thesis 17 of 54 (c15yc) against 28 of 54 (c8), difference -20.4 points, 90% interval (-34.6, -4.8): inconclusive under the frozen rule; retention 49 against 49: proceed. The rule required both to proceed, so c15yc does not go on.\n  4888\t- **Decided (by the rule the council fixed before the send, D440; no new judgement):** the combined Step 1 candidate c15yc stops; c8 stays in force. The year change moved its error to a neighbouring case (capex years separated, the memory question pushed from the ruler's 2027-against-2026 shape to 2026), so under D391 it is not tuned further on these articles. Change 2 alone (the scoped capacity counterexample) is not carried as its own version without a council decision: its measured target without change 1 is one doubtful aggregate in 729 c8 calls.\n  4889\t- **Next:** the council chooses the next step toward the PRD's production goal (D439).\n  4890\t\n 10125\t## D681 · 2026-11-20 · Alex opens the hybrid system's build and test; phase 1 is a new judge version (J2) for the judge's reasoning errors\n 10126\t\n 10127\t- Alex, 2026-11-20, after the merge test (D680) and the finding that the old system loses on the 32 matters at opening and in the judge's\n 10128\t  reasoning, not in reading: \"不是聊了半天就是要合并两边最好的来提升系统吗？\"; then, on the proposal to fix the judge's reasoning errors\n 10129\t  first as a new judge version, with a council review and a test of a few cents: \"可以啊，你现在开始做hybrid system 的构建和测试，不要犯了和做新系统一样的错误到最后才发现问题\".\n 10130\t- Decided (his words): the hybrid system is built and tested. The judge (judging-v7, frozen by D354) may get a new version, J2, measured\n 10131\t  against v7. The frozen ruler is unchanged.\n 10132\t- The plan (`docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md`) guards against the new system's mistakes:\n 10133\t  - a change is accepted by its effect on final answers, read by blind readers;\n 10134\t  - an end-to-end slice runs in week 1;\n 10135\t  - the attainable verdict is computed first;\n 10136\t  - every line has a source;\n 10137\t  - the design uses the stored dev failures, and acceptance is on a fresh window.\n 10138\t- Attainable on the 32 matters (computed first):\n 10139\t  - the judge fix can add M08 and M14 to old's 10;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,re,collections; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import judge_probe as p; from hivemind.views import judging; cs=json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"cases.json\\\").read_text()); flags=json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"hidden-flags.json\\\").read_text()); result=collections.Counter(); details={}; picks={\\\"T-old-3-Q3\\\",\\\"T-new-2-Q20\\\",\\\"T-old-2-Q29\\\",\\\"T-old-2-Q16\\\",\\\"C-new-3-Q33\\\",\\\"C-old-2-Q15\\\",\\\"T-new-2-Q31\\\",\\\"T-new-2-Q27\\\",\\\"T-old-3-Q33\\\"};\nfor c in cs:\n n=c[\\\"case\\\"]; j,q,_,b=p.stored(c); s=q[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"]; z=p.without_previous(s); f=flags[n]; hide=re.search(r\\\"\\\\[Not shown: (\\\\d+)\\\",s); assert bool(hide)==f[\\\"hidden\\\"] and (\\\"[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]\\\" in s)==f[\\\"had_previous\\\"]; assert judging.evidence_shown_in(s)==judging.evidence_shown_in(z);\n opts={};\n for arm in (\\\"v7\\\",\\\"v7-noprev\\\",\\\"J2b-noprev\\\"):\n  paths=[p.OUT/\\\"probe\\\"/arm/(\\\"{}-{}.json\\\".format(n,k)) for k in (1,2,3)]; answers=[json.loads(pp.read_text())[\\\"answer\\\"] for pp in paths if pp.exists()]; moved=len(answers)==3 and sum(x[\\\"rung\\\"]\"'!=j[\"rung\"] for x in answers)>=2; result[(c[\"role\"],\"hidden\" if f[\"hidden\"] else \"clean\",f[\"had_previous\"],arm,\"complete\")]+=len(answers)==3; result[(c[\"role\"],\"hidden\" if f[\"hidden\"] else \"clean\",f[\"had_previous\"],arm,\"moved\")]+=moved\n  if n in picks and arm != \"J2b-noprev\": opts[arm]=[(x[\"rung\"],x[\"implied_outcome\"][:260]) for x in answers];\n if n in picks:\n  print(n,\"hidden\",int(hide[1]) if hide else 0,\"original\",j[\"rung\"],s.splitlines()[0][:280]); print(opts)\nprint(*result.items(),sep=\"'\"\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,re,collections; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import judge_probe as p; from hivemind.views import judging; cs=json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"cases.json\\\").read_text()); flags=json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"hidden-flags.json\\\").read_text()); result=collections.Counter(); details={}; picks={\\\"T-old-3-Q3\\\",\\\"T-new-2-Q20\\\",\\\"T-old-2-Q29\\\",\\\"T-old-2-Q16\\\",\\\"C-new-3-Q33\\\",\\\"C-old-2-Q15\\\",\\\"T-new-2-Q31\\\",\\\"T-new-2-Q27\\\",\\\"T-old-3-Q33\\\"};\nfor c in cs:\n n=c[\\\"case\\\"]; j,q,_,b=p.stored(c); s=q[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"]; z=p.without_previous(s); f=flags[n]; hide=re.search(r\\\"\\\\[Not shown: (\\\\d+)\\\",s); assert bool(hide)==f[\\\"hidden\\\"] and (\\\"[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]\\\" in s)==f[\\\"had_previous\\\"]; assert judging.evidence_shown_in(s)==judging.evidence_shown_in(z);\n opts={};\n for arm in (\\\"v7\\\",\\\"v7-noprev\\\",\\\"J2b-noprev\\\"):\n  paths=[p.OUT/\\\"probe\\\"/arm/(\\\"{}-{}.json\\\".format(n,k)) for k in (1,2,3)]; answers=[json.loads(pp.read_text())[\\\"answer\\\"] for pp in paths if pp.exists()]; moved=len(answers)==3 and sum(x[\\\"rung\\\"]\"'!=j[\"rung\"] for x in answers)>=2; result[(c[\"role\"],\"hidden\" if f[\"hidden\"] else \"clean\",f[\"had_previous\"],arm,\"complete\")]+=len(answers)==3; result[(c[\"role\"],\"hidden\" if f[\"hidden\"] else \"clean\",f[\"had_previous\"],arm,\"moved\")]+=moved\n  if n in picks and arm != \"J2b-noprev\": opts[arm]=[(x[\"rung\"],x[\"implied_outcome\"][:260]) for x in answers];\n if n in picks:\n  print(n,\"hidden\",int(hide[1]) if hide else 0,\"original\",j[\"rung\"],s.splitlines()[0][:280]); print(opts)\nprint(*result.items(),sep=\"'\"\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"T-new-2-Q20 hidden 0 original 3 Thesis v32 (ai-capex, theme, focus \"AI-infrastructure debt's share of net new investment-grade bond issuance in calendar 2026 (the item reports as much as 30% in some indexes) and whether that issuance continues to clear against multi-decade-high sovereign yields and 6%-plus long\n{'v7': [(3, 'Roughly 28%: carry forward the prior estimate based on S&P’s reported $225 billion issued through July and its projection of $400 billion by year-end, calibrated against the reported up-to-30% share in some IG indexes. The evidence does not establish that all '), (3, \"Roughly 28%, retaining the broad S&P segment tally's year-end projection as the best full-year indicator; no new evidence gives a quantified change to that estimate or a replacement denominator.\"), (3, 'Roughly 28% for calendar 2026, retaining the prior broader-market estimate based on the S&P-related segment’s $225 billion issued by end-July and its projection of $400 billion by year-end compared with net new investment-grade issuance. The latest evidence do')], 'v7-noprev': [(3, 'Approximately 30%. The most direct share estimate is e2318; the $225 billion issued through July and possible $400 billion by year-end in the broader hyperscaler-and-related-company segment (e2360) supports substantial issuance, but does not by itself yield th'), (3, \"A roughly 25–30% share is the best implied range, with the reported figure near 30% for some indexes. The $225 billion issued through July and S&P's potential $400 billion year-end segment total support substantial issuance, but the evidence gives no comparabl\"), (3, \"Approximately 25%–30%, with the available direct benchmark near 30%: S&P's roughly $225 billion issued by end-July and possible $400 billion by year-end indicate substantial supply, while the evidence does not provide the full-year net-new-IG denominator neede\")]}\nT-new-2-Q27 hidden 0 original 3 Thesis v42 (us-china-tariffs, theme, focus \"A formal U.S. tariff action on semiconductors (presidential proclamation / Federal Register notice, e.g. under Section 232 or IEEPA) or an explicit administration decision not to impose such duties, and the scope of any duties.\", 2027, \n{'v7': [(3, 'Still open on 2027-01-31: the most likely outcome is that no qualifying formal tariff action and no formal abandonment has occurred. The evidence supplies no tariff rate or timing from which to infer a different outcome.'), (3, 'The most likely outcome is still open on January 31, 2027: no qualifying formal tariff action and no formal abandonment after August 27, 2026. The report says tariffs were being considered, but provides no action date or tariff schedule, and the White House re'), (3, 'Most likely, neither a formal tariff action nor a formal abandonment will have occurred by January 31, 2027. The August 27 report only says tariffs are being considered, while the White House statement is not a formal decision; neither establishes rung 1 or 2.')], 'v7-noprev': [(3, 'Most likely, no qualifying formal action and no formal abandonment will have occurred by January 31, 2027, leaving the initiative open (rung 3). The report of consideration is a weak signal toward action, but supplies no concrete timing or scope and is counter'), (3, 'The evidence implies that the status is most likely still unresolved on January 31, 2027: the only report describes tariffs as under consideration, while the White House official disclaims reporting absent an official announcement. No formal action or formal a'), (3, 'By January 31, 2027, the most likely outcome is no qualifying formal action and no formal abandonment, leaving the question open at rung 3. The report of consideration modestly raises the possibility of action but does not establish that a proclamation or offi')]}\nT-new-2-Q31 hidden 0 original 1 Thesis v52 (ai-capex, theme, focus \"Contracted/deployed AI data-center capacity in Australia built on NVIDIA's DSX platform by end-2027 versus the up-to-2 GW target, and the implied NVIDIA GPU / AI-factory demand from that buildout.\", 2027, due 2028-03-30): How many gigawatts of \n{'v7': [(2, 'Below 1.5 GW by December 31, 2027; the disclosures do not support a tighter quantified estimate of eligible, non-duplicated capacity. The 2 GW figure is an upper target, while the quantified CDC and IREN project figures are not established as additional, fully'), (2, \"About 0.8 GW by December 31, 2027: start from the 72 MW NVIDIA collaboration and give discounted, partial credit to the 800 MW IREN Bundey development and CDC's 800 MW under construction, since neither full figure is established as Australian DSX capacity deli\"), (2, \"Roughly 0.1GW of qualifying capacity by December 31, 2027, anchored by IREN's signed 72MW NVIDIA compute collaboration and rounded to about 0.1GW. The 800MW Bundey and CDC figures are not fully countable as DSX capacity under binding deployment contracts, and \")], 'v7-noprev': [(2, 'About 1.0 GW by December 31, 2027. This is a discounted forecast from the 2 GW coalition-wide ceiling, reflecting the absence of partner-level allocations or schedules and the fact that some cited partner capacity is broader portfolio capacity rather than conf'), (2, \"About 0.8 GW by December 31, 2027. This discounts the unallocated, multi-partner up-to-2-GW target for the absence of deployment schedules or sized binding commitments, while giving some weight to CDC's 800 MW under construction as broader portfolio evidence r\"), (2, \"About 1.0 GW by December 31, 2027. I treat IREN's 800 MW Bundey campus as a development footprint, not as 800 MW certain to be deployed or bindingly contracted by the cutoff; I give partial credit for delivery and for CDC's 800 MW under construction, while not\")]}\nC-new-3-Q33 hidden 0 original 4 Thesis v44 (ai-capex, theme, focus \"Total global AI venture capital funding raised in calendar 2026, versus the >$400 billion NVIDIA's CFO cites for H1 2026 and the $265 billion raised in all of 2025, and the share directed to compute.\", 2026, due 2027-03-31): How much total glob\n{'v7': [(4, \"Around $650 billion, but below it: the reported H1 amount exceeds $400 billion, while a rough continuation of August's $42 billion monthly pace for all global venture funding implies less than about $252 billion of additional AI funding over six months because\"), (4, \"About $600 billion for calendar 2026, rung 4: NVIDIA's report of more than $400 billion in H1 implies over $800 billion if that pace continued, while August's $42 billion in all-sector venture funding implies roughly $252 billion for a six-month remainder at t\"), (4, \"Near but below $650bn for calendar 2026: start with NVIDIA's claim of more than $400bn in H1, then use the August all-market pace of $42bn/month as roughly $252bn of possible total-market funding over H2; AI is only a share of that H2 amount.\")], 'v7-noprev': [(5, 'NVIDIA said AI venture funding exceeded $400 billion in H1 2026. Annualizing that six-month pace implies more than $800 billion for 2026, placing the forecast in rung 5; reaching its $650 billion floor would require only a further $250 billion in H2.'), (5, 'About $800 billion or more for calendar 2026, derived by carrying the reported H1 pace of more than $400 billion through H2. That annualized pace is in rung 5.'), (5, \"NVIDIA's cited H1 2026 total exceeded $400 billion; carrying that six-month funding pace through the calendar year implies more than $800 billion for 2026, before the additional disclosed H2 financings. That run-rate is in rung 5 (at least $650 billion).\")]}\nT-old-2-Q16 hidden 47 original 1 Thesis v16 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA total CPU revenue in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027?\n{'v7': [(1, 'About $25 billion or modestly above: carry NVIDIA’s roughly $20 billion standalone Vera outlook forward and add Grace at an approximately $5 billion-plus annual run-rate, based on its reported trailing-12-month revenue. That puts the central estimate just over'), (1, \"Approximately $25 billion or slightly more: the roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone Vera outlook plus Grace CPU revenue running above $5 billion on a trailing-12-month basis. This narrowly exceeds rung 1's $25 billion threshold, with some uncertainty because\"), (3, 'Approximately $20 billion in FY2027: the direct total-CPU outlook is the anchor. Grace’s reported greater-than-$5-billion trailing-12-month revenue is not added wholesale because it is historical and the management outlook is already stated as total CPU revenu')], 'v7-noprev': [(2, 'About $20 billion of standalone Vera revenue plus roughly $5 billion at the reported Grace trailing-12-month run-rate implies approximately $25 billion of total CPU revenue in FY2027.'), (1, 'About $25 billion or slightly more: carry the reported Grace CPU revenue run-rate of more than $5 billion over the trailing 12 months into FY2027 and add the approximately $20 billion standalone Vera expectation. This is above the $25 billion rung-1 boundary.'), (1, 'About $20 billion of standalone Vera CPU revenue plus a roughly $5 billion-or-more Grace revenue run-rate implies total FY2027 CPU revenue around $25 billion or slightly above. The additive estimate is at or just above the rung-1 threshold of more than $25 bil')]}\nT-old-2-Q29 hidden 52 original 3 Thesis v29 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA's committed equity investments in ecosystem partners\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\n{'v7': [(3, 'Approximately $54 billion at the FY2027 annual report: $25 billion reported as committed at July 26, plus $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027, the $3.5 billion MediaTek investment announced afterward, and risk-adjusted amounts for the reported $1'), (3, 'About $58–62 billion at the FY2027 annual-report date: start from the disclosed $25 billion commitment balance plus $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027, then add the post-snapshot $3.5 billion MediaTek investment and a discounted contribution from the'), (3, 'Approximately $51 billion at the FY2027 annual report: the $25 billion commitment balance plus $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027, plus the $3.5 billion MediaTek investment announced afterward, gives $46.5 billion; adding about $4.5 billion as a')], 'v7-noprev': [(2, 'Roughly $30–40 billion of commitments at the FY2027 report, derived from the $25 billion reported balance and the subsequent disclosed remaining-year commitments and investments, while allowing for commitments to be funded before year-end and avoiding double-c'), (2, 'About $47 billion: start with $25 billion reported, add the $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027, and include the later $3.5 billion MediaTek convertible-bond investment as a potential equity commitment; discount the uncommitted investment discuss'), (2, \"Approximately $43 billion: add NVIDIA's reported $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027 to the $25 billion reported as of July 26. That is within rung 2 ($25 billion to below $50 billion).\")]}\nC-old-2-Q15 hidden 74 original 5 Thesis v15 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA supply commitments\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much will NVIDIA's supply commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\n{'v7': [(5, 'About $215 billion at publication: approximately $187 billion of scheduled commitments remain after the $92 billion FY2027 amount runs off, plus an estimated $28 billion of replenishment to secure supply against expected demand.'), (5, 'About $215 billion at publication: subtract the $92 billion scheduled for the rest of FY2027 from the $279 billion disclosed total to get a $187 billion residual, then add an estimated $28 billion of replenishment. That is above the $200 billion rung-5 boundar'), (5, 'About $215 billion at publication: the $279 billion disclosed total less $92 billion scheduled for the rest of FY2027 leaves about $187 billion; an estimated roughly $28 billion of replenishment, supported by continued supply securing and the higher sales outl')], 'v7-noprev': [(2, 'About $187 billion on the disclosed schedule: subtract the $92 billion scheduled for the remainder of FY2027 from the $279 billion total, leaving the FY2028-and-later commitments. No quantified evidence supports adding enough new commitments to cross $200 bill'), (5, 'About $187 billion of the disclosed $279 billion schedule falls beyond FY2027 after subtracting the $92 billion scheduled for the rest of FY2027. Given the recent $160 billion increase and continuing demand and supply-growth signals, the most likely FY2027 rep'), (4, 'About $187 billion: subtract the $92 billion scheduled for the remainder of FY2027 from the $279 billion total, leaving $87 billion for FY2028, $88 billion for FY2029, and $12 billion for FY2030 and later. This is below $200 billion and sits at rung 4.')]}\nT-old-3-Q3 hidden 2264 original 1 Thesis v3 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA total revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\n{'v7': [(1, 'About $446 billion: $177.837 billion reported in the first half, roughly $113.6 billion for Q3 using the 3.1% average beat over the high end of guidance, and about $127 billion for Q4 by carrying forward 12% sequential growth, plus the previously derived $27–2'), (1, 'About $445–446 billion: $177.837 billion in first-half revenue plus roughly $113.6 billion for Q3 using the $108 billion guide and the observed 3.1% average beat over guidance high ends, plus roughly $127 billion for Q4 carrying forward 12% sequential growth, '), (1, 'Roughly $445 billion: $177.837 billion reported in the first half, about $113.6 billion for Q3 using the $108 billion guide and the observed 3.1% average beat over guidance, and about $127 billion for Q4 carrying forward 12% sequential growth, total roughly $4')], 'v7-noprev': [(2, 'About $410 billion: Q1 and Q2 were $81.62 billion and $96.2 billion; Q3 guidance is $108 billion; and 65% Q4 year-over-year growth applied to an approximately $75 billion FY2026 Q4 baseline implies about $124 billion for Q4. The resulting total is approximatel'), (2, 'About $410 billion: $177.837 billion for the first half (e2754), plus the $108 billion Q3 midpoint (e2715), plus roughly $124 billion for Q4. The Q4 estimate applies the reported 65% growth expectation (e5192) to an implied FY2026 Q4 base of about $75 billion,'), (2, 'About $405–$411 billion: first-half revenue was $177.8 billion, Q3 is guided at $108 billion (with a specific third-party estimate of $113–$114 billion), and Q4 growth expectations support roughly $114–$120 billion. This is above $392 billion but below the $43')]}\nT-old-3-Q33 hidden 64 original 3 Thesis v33 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA equity investment commitments\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of equity investment commitments will NVIDIA report as outstanding or committed?\n{'v7': [(3, 'About $43 billion at the FY2027 filing, derived from the reported $25 billion commitment balance plus the $18 billion remainder-of-year commitment. The separate $42 billion of first-half equity spending is investment already made, not an additional outstanding'), (3, 'About $43 billion at the FY2027 annual filing, derived from the $25 billion reported as of July 26 plus the $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027. This remains within rung 3 and below the $50 billion boundary for rung 4.'), (3, 'About $43 billion at the FY2027 filing: the reported $25 billion balance plus the $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027. This is the best quantified bridge; the reported first-half investment spending and later deal amounts do not establish an additiona')], 'v7-noprev': [(2, 'Approximately $20 billion outstanding or committed at the FY2027 filing. This starts from the reported $25 billion balance, allows for deployment of the $18 billion identified for the rest of FY2027 and some run-off, while continued investment activity partly '), (2, 'Around $18 billion at the FY2027 filing, with the disclosed $25 billion as of July 26 providing an upper nearby anchor. The $18 billion remainder-of-year commitment is the most directly relevant forward amount; the much larger investment and deal figures do no'), (2, 'Approximately $25 billion outstanding or committed at the FY2027 annual filing, based on the latest reported $25 billion balance; the $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027 indicates substantial activity but does not establish a net addition to the balan')]}\n(('target', 'clean', True, 'v7', 'complete'), 7)\n(('target', 'clean', True, 'v7', 'moved'), 1)\n(('target', 'clean', True, 'v7-noprev', 'complete'), 7)\n(('target', 'clean', True, 'v7-noprev', 'moved'), 3)\n(('target', 'clean', True, 'J2b-noprev', 'complete'), 6)\n(('target', 'clean', True, 'J2b-noprev', 'moved'), 2)\n(('control', 'hidden', True, 'v7', 'complete'), 18)\n(('control', 'hidden', True, 'v7', 'moved'), 0)\n(('control', 'hidden', True, 'v7-noprev', 'complete'), 18)\n(('control', 'hidden', True, 'v7-noprev', 'moved'), 1)\n(('control', 'hidden', True, 'J2b-noprev', 'complete'), 12)\n(('control', 'hidden', True, 'J2b-noprev', 'moved'), 1)\n(('control', 'clean', True, 'v7', 'complete'), 5)\n(('control', 'clean', True, 'v7', 'moved'), 0)\n(('control', 'clean', True, 'v7-noprev', 'complete'), 5)\n(('control', 'clean', True, 'v7-noprev', 'moved'), 1)\n(('control', 'clean', True, 'J2b-noprev', 'complete'), 5)\n(('control', 'clean', True, 'J2b-noprev', 'moved'), 1)\n(('target', 'hidden', True, 'v7', 'complete'), 16)\n(('target', 'hidden', True, 'v7', 'moved'), 1)\n(('target', 'hidden', True, 'v7-noprev', 'complete'), 16)\n(('target', 'hidden', True, 'v7-noprev', 'moved'), 11)\n(('target', 'hidden', True, 'J2b-noprev', 'complete'), 9)\n(('target', 'hidden', True, 'J2b-noprev', 'moved'), 7)\n(('target', 'clean', False, 'v7', 'complete'), 1)\n(('target', 'clean', False, 'v7', 'moved'), 0)\n(('target', 'clean', 