{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"**Stop J2a and J2b as candidates. Result 3 shows that removing the previous answer changes forecasts. It leaves open whether those changes improve them.**\n\n- **Result 3.** The code keeps every visible item and removes the prior answer and the notice about omitted evidence. Ten of the 12 extra target moves came from requests with omitted evidence. Among the seven targets with a previous answer and nothing hidden, moves rose from one to three. Q29 moved in all three repeats, yet two still added the disputed $25B and $18B. [judge_probe.py:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:129)\n- **Next test.** Use (a). The cap of 100 hidden items gives 13 targets and eight controls. Restore only evidence in force at the original cutoff. Send three paired repeats with and without the prior answer. Compare full and clipped evidence in the no-prior arms to test what restoring evidence changes. Predeclare a screen of five net target repairs, jointly supported in two of three repeats, with no lost controls or extra refusals. Rung-only also discards whatever information the prior reasons carried.\n- **D198.** Alex can choose to keep the same prior content and change its presentation, approve a separate summary of omitted evidence with the prior forecast removed, or approve showing the full evidence. The first preserves D198. The latter two change how omitted evidence is carried and need a new decision from Alex or the council under D439 while he is away. [DECISIONS-log.md:2559](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2559)\n- **Reading.** Yes, for diagnosis. Include all repeats of moved cases and controls, plus a preselected matched unmoved sample. Shuffle them with stored answers and v7 re-sends, showing what each answer actually received. Finish the 432-card reading for the record. Neither arm can recover rule (c) through that reading. On d3-q18, J2b picked Yes three times and gave weight to the NVL576 timeline when asked about NVL144. [DESIGN-J2.md:191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:191)\n\nDISAGREE: Retire both J2 arms and test the previous answer on identical, complete evidence before changing D198."}}
